6.steps:
1. Add a custom zone test of trusted or public security type and assign an interface say x2 to it;
2.	Locate the server on the x2 subnet, create two address objects ftp_private and ftp_public for the servers private and public address on the Network->Address Objects page;
2.	Set up a dns server A on the wan side, create an entry with domain name ftp.test.com resolved to the servers public ip address;
3.	On the NAT policies page, add a custom policy as below:
Original source: x2 subnet
Translated source:wan interface ip
Original destination:ftp_public
Translated destination:ftp_private
Original service:ftp
Translated service:original
Inbound interface:Any
Outbound interface:Any
Click the ok button after completed;
4.	On the firewall, Add an allow access rule from wan->test with destination ftp_public for ftp service of all users;
5.	From another host on the x2 subnet( set A as its dns server), try to access the ftp server: ftp://ftp.test.com
6.	Test above steps for http, ping, smtp, pop3,telnet service etc.
